-- A rule that shares its name with a record. WITH names fields, which is what
-- lets a site tell the two apart; WITHAL names none, so it cannot choose, and
-- what the author reads is the ordinary "multiple definitions" error. A
-- default must not be what decides which definition was meant (R8, as for a
-- WITH: TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md T1, ruled by Meng 2026-10-09).

DECLARE Paint
  HAS label IS A STRING TYPICALLY "plain"

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
Paint MEANS n

#EVAL Paint WITHAL
